### 💡 Key Design Decisions for a Lightweight MAID

* **Use MCP (Model Context Protocol) as the Glue:** Instead of writing massive custom APIs, make each of your parallel services expose an MCP server. Roo Code (or Cline), Headroom, and OmniRoute all natively support MCP. This keeps service-to-service communication highly standardized and incredibly fast.
* **Combine OmniRoute and Headroom as a "Double Proxy":** 
  Let MAID point its LLM requests to **Headroom** (running on a local port). Headroom will compress the prompts/tools, and then forward the slimmed-down payload to **OmniRoute** (running on another local port). OmniRoute will then use its smart routing to execute the call via the cheapest or fastest provider. This maximizes speed and minimizes cost.
* **Avoid Monolithic Agent Loops:** Keep your agent logic in LangGraph simple and stateless where possible. Offload heavy operations (like terminal execution and browser actions) to the Dockerized OpenHands sandbox, treating it strictly as an external utility rather than a core part of the orchestrator's state.

